	)
	(text "Simulated ref.: 4.5V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 79.248 80.01 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2920b325-4d8b-486d-9967-75bfc0e28151")
	)
	(text "Simulated ref.: 1V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 79.756 136.398 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3280e933-6353-42aa-b6b6-35969a9990da")
	)
	(text "Controls the target voltage for each stage of the envelope.\n\nDuring the attack, the comparator outputs +9V,\nwhich goes through the diode and to the next part.\n\nDuring the decay, the comparator outputs -9V.\nHowever, the diode blocks that, and the target voltage\nis pulled down to the sustain voltage.\n\nThe release is the same as the decay,\nexcept the pulldown voltage is GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 131.572 28.448 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "395fb14f-56fe-4925-81a2-bd4228dc19a6")
	)
	(text "Controls attack length.\n\nUtilizes a high pass filter to turn the incoming pulse signal\ninto a controlled positive burst of voltage. The diode blocks\nthe negative burst of voltage from the pulse's falling edge.\n\nThe burst creates the attack by making the comparator output\nhigh (+9V) when it's above the comparator's ref. voltage.\n\nHow long (time-wise) the attack lasts is controlled\nby the trim pots. The left two control the burst's slope,\nwhile the right one controls the comparator's ref. voltage."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 59.69 27.178 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3f1272ac-5dcc-4f99-89ed-d04dfb58d833")
	)
	(text "Simulated resistance = 5k"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 180.34 44.704 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6a9a717b-be4f-4fbc-bd52-c58d4cee3b00")
	)
	(text "Simulated resistance = 60k each"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 52.07 74.676 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8e969266-d742-438e-beeb-4535a593eab7")
	)
	(text "Controls the slope of the attack, decay, and release.\n\nUtilizes a low pass filter with two cutoff freqs. depending \non if the target voltage is currently higher than the output.\n\nAs it turns out, the target voltage is higher than the output\nonly during the attack, so in effect this separates the attack's\nslope from the decay's and release's.\n\nHowever, this means that the decay and release are the same."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204.47 28.448 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "9b890312-c41f-48f8-9a27-db5e0257c1ce")
	)
	(text "Simulated resistance = 200k"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.832 133.604 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "b9cbcc3d-d59e-4c04-82af-a04340f2bd03")
	)
	(text "Simulated resistance = 50k"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.832 100.076 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "c7d017ee-4469-47e6-b211-fcbb2d644de0")
	)
	(text "A high resistance in the left two pots can filter the input signal, \nwhich causes the envelope to distort if the input signal is fast.\nHowever, a low resistance makes the pulse too short to be detected.\n\nTherefore, adjusting the right pot is preferred."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 60.452 92.202 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f8f374aa-740a-4ec3-8fbf-3841ab42cff8")
	)
